# Fault W-B-1: a scenario world re-checked the base's own asks: the base's `a: x[2026-02]`, made random only by the
# scenario's `replace rule`, refused the whole scenario `LOAD-RANDOM`. L §6.4 The base is whole without its scenarios:
# "every ask is checked only in the worlds its line is evaluated in (§5.18)"; the ask a is in the base world, where x is 1
# (a); and the scenario's rule, brought by its version, is inside the scenario and reads its def r ("A read of an item
# declared in a scenario file is allowed only inside that scenario", L §6.4). b is a paths mean (its value is the
# paths', not asserted).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "a source"

def x[k in months]: num at start_of(k)
  rule base = 1

ask a: x[2026-02]
=== s.tally
scenario s over m
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

input mu: num question "mean?"

def r: dist = poisson(mu)

version w
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  mu = 0.5 "row"

version v
  cite src
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace rule x.drawn beats base = r

ask b: mean(x[2026-02]) in s law 2026-06-30 paths 10 seed 1
=== expect
a: 1
  cut 2026-01-01
b: ...
  world: s
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
